---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Diagram from '../components/Diagram.astro';
import { site, work } from '../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout>
  <Header />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero shell" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-main">
        <div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> SOFTWARE ENGINEER <span class="eyebrow-separator">/</span> BACKEND & DISTRIBUTED SYSTEMS</div>
        <h1 id="hero-title">Engineering systems<br/>that <span class="accent-text">hold up.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-description">I'm <strong>Priyansh Sharma</strong> — a software engineer focused on designing reliable backend systems, distributed processing architectures, and practical AI-powered developer tools.</p>
        <div class="hero-buttons"><a class="button button-primary" href="#work">Explore selected work <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button button-secondary" href={site.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        <div class="hero-bottom"><div class="hero-meta"><span class="small-label">CURRENTLY</span><span>Software Engineer II · Thales</span></div><div class="hero-meta"><span class="small-label">FOCUS</span><span>Architecture · Reliability · Scale</span></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-aside"><div class="side-index"><span>01 / INTRODUCTION</span><span class="thin-rule"></span><span>EST. 2023</span></div><Diagram /><div class="hero-aside-caption"><span><span class="pulse-dot"></span> SYSTEMS THINKING</span><span>DESIGN → BUILD → VERIFY</span></div></div>
    </section>
    <section class="ticker" aria-label="Technical areas"><div class="shell ticker-inner"><span>JAVA / JVM</span><span>↗</span><span>DISTRIBUTED SYSTEMS</span><span>↗</span><span>FAULT TOLERANCE</span><span>↗</span><span>DATA PROCESSING</span><span>↗</span><span>AI ENGINEERING</span></div></section>
    <section class="work-section shell section-spacing" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-title"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="section-kicker">01 <span class="kicker-rule"></span> SELECTED ENGINEERING WORK</p><h2 id="work-title">Built for complexity.<br/><span class="muted-heading">Designed for clarity.</span></h2></div><p class="section-intro">A selection of systems and engineering problems I've worked on. Detailed technical write-ups are being prepared with careful attention to confidentiality and verifiable evidence.</p></div>
      <div class="work-grid">{work.map((item) => <article class="work-card"><div class="card-top"><span class="card-number">{item.number} / 03</span><span class="card-marker" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><div class="card-graphic" aria-hidden="true"><span class="graphic-orbit graphic-orbit-one"></span><span class="graphic-orbit graphic-orbit-two"></span><span class="graphic-core">{item.number}</span><span class="graphic-crosshair">+</span></div><span class="card-category">{item.category}</span><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.description}</p><div class="card-tags">{item.tags.map(tag => <span>{tag}</span>)}</div><div class="card-footer"><span class="draft-indicator"></span>{item.status}</div></article>)}</div>
      <div class="section-footnote"><span>NOTE / 001</span><p>These are summaries, not published technical case studies. Deep dives and evidence will be added after review.</p></div>
    </section>
    <section class="about-band" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title"><div class="shell about-layout"><div><p class="section-kicker">02 <span class="kicker-rule"></span> THE ENGINEER BEHIND THE SYSTEMS</p><h2 id="about-title">I care about what<br/><span class="accent-text">happens in production.</span></h2></div><div class="about-copy"><p>Good engineering goes beyond getting something to work. It means understanding what happens under load, how systems recover from failure, and which tradeoffs are worth making.</p><p>My work spans backend services, distributed processing, orchestration, and developer tooling. I enjoy making complex systems easier to reason about — and more dependable to operate.</p><a class="text-link" href={site.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore my experience on LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
    <section class="approach-section shell section-spacing" id="approach" aria-labelledby="approach-title"><p class="section-kicker">03 <span class="kicker-rule"></span> HOW I THINK</p><div class="section-heading approach-heading"><h2 id="approach-title">Principles over<br/><span class="muted-heading">buzzwords.</span></h2><p class="section-intro">The questions that guide how I approach engineering problems.</p></div><div class="principle-grid"><article><span>01 /</span><h3>Reason about failure.</h3><p>What breaks under contention, partial failure, retries, or unexpected inputs? Design recovery as part of the system.</p></article><article><span>02 /</span><h3>Make tradeoffs explicit.</h3><p>Choose the simplest architecture that meets real constraints. Understand the complexity introduced by every abstraction.</p></article><article><span>03 /</span><h3>Measure what matters.</h3><p>Use tests, representative workloads, and observability to support conclusions rather than relying on assumptions.</p></article></div></section>
    <section class="contact-section" id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title"><div class="shell contact-layout"><div><p class="section-kicker">04 <span class="kicker-rule"></span> CONNECT</p><h2 id="contact-title">Let's build something<br/><span class="accent-text">that matters.</span></h2><p>Interested in backend engineering, distributed systems, or a technical conversation? I'd be glad to connect.</p></div><div class="contact-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href={site.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Connect on LinkedIn ↗</a><a class="button button-secondary" href={site.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore GitHub ↗</a></div></div></section>
  </main>
  <footer class="site-footer"><div class="shell footer-layout"><a class="footer-brand" href="/">PS<span>.</span></a><span>© {new Date().getFullYear()} Priyansh Sharma. Built with intention.</span><a href="#main">BACK TO TOP ↑</a></div></footer>
</BaseLayout>
